  "name": "physics",
  "map": "Victoria Road: Ellinia",
  "description": "The physics schedule (#397): measures the movement physics on Ellinia, from the bottom of the map. Walk speed on the ground's long walk; climb speed on a rope (x -316) and a ladder (x 627); the jump arc and flight time on two gap jumps, three times each way; whether a jump off a rope rises; drops of 91, 258, 424 and 480 virtual px (480 is DROP_REACH); and the teleport reach sideways and up. Teleport down is never planned, so no Trial can cast it. Every batch but 'teleport' plans without the teleport skill, so a teleporting class measures walks and jumps too; the 'teleport' batch needs a character with Teleport. Each Trial's 'measures' says what the analyzer reads it for: python -m maple.calibration.analysis <record>. Coordinates are the feet, in virtual px; tolerances are virtual px.",
